      "side": 1,
      "message": "Does [`phandle-array`](https://docs.zephyrproject.org/latest/build/dts/phandles.html#id8) type work?\n\nUpstream I found the `st,stm32-rtc` node has a property type that mixes phandles and data values.\n\nExample from the 96b_carbon board.  The `clocks` property is defined by the [base.yaml file](https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/blob/6c25136e604ae54f332d60458bc604c71cb5f070/dts/bindings/base/base.yaml#L55C7-L55C7).\n\n```\nrtc: rtc@40002800 {\n  compatible \u003d \"st,stm32-rtc\";\n  reg \u003d \u003c 0x40002800 0x400 \u003e;\n  interrupts \u003d \u003c 0x29 0x0 \u003e;\n  clocks \u003d \u003c \u0026rcc 0x40 0x10000000 \u003e, \u003c \u0026rcc 0x5 0x26870 \u003e;\n  prescaler \u003d \u003c 0x8000 \u003e;\n  status \u003d \"okay\";\n  bbram: backup_regs {\n    compatible \u003d \"st,stm32-bbram\";\n    st,backup-regs \u003d \u003c 0x14 \u003e;\n    status \u003d \"disabled\";\n  };\n};\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 38,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 38,
        "endChar": 78
